    "info": {
      "description": "This file is generated from mixed sources.  Chamber from a Manson / Reyneke print.  Cartridge by guess work reducing some dimensions just enough to allow the case to chamber.  Manson prints are a mix of SAAMI and CIP parameters, thus making exact duplication a bit difficult.  The drawing specifies a .075\" freebore but also says freebore is to allow a 75 ELD-M bullet to be forward of the neck/shoulder junction.  .075\" does not seem long enough to provide this requirement, so it is assumed the freebore is to be established after the chamber is reamed by the use of a separate throating reamer.\r",
